Subject: Do not download a cluster-matched kubectl at runtime

Origin: DHI-internal (runtime dependency policy)
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/kubeflow/pipelines 555bfa60a70da88c594960bdacfd78fa7c061043
Verify: cmd `go test ./package/main/kubeflow-pipelines-cache-deployer/tests -run TestClosureRoot -count=1` expect "ok"
Forwarded: no (upstream offers no switch to turn the download off)
Drop-When: never: upstream calls the download unconditionally; revisit if upstream adds a way to turn it off

deploy-cache-service.sh calls install_version_matched_kubectl before it talks to
the cluster. That function asks the API server for its version, fetches the
matching stable kubectl from dl.k8s.io into $HOME/bin and puts it first on PATH.
The package declares a pinned kubectl line as a runtime dependency instead, so a
running deployer never executes a binary it fetched itself and needs neither curl
nor jq. Only the call is removed; the function definitions stay so the change
against upstream remains a single line.

--- a/backend/src/cache/deployer/deploy-cache-service.sh
+++ b/backend/src/cache/deployer/deploy-cache-service.sh
@@ -72,8 +72,6 @@
 MUTATING_WEBHOOK_CONFIGURATION_NAME="cache-webhook-${NAMESPACE}"
 WEBHOOK_SECRET_NAME=webhook-server-tls
 
-install_version_matched_kubectl
-
 # This should fail if there are connectivity problems
 # Gotcha: Listing all objects requires list permission,
 # but when listing a single oblect kubectl will fail if it's not found
